 "sq": [
  {
   "_id": 9361,
   "ANSWER": "<p>Functional programming relies on pure functions and immutable data, ensuring predictable outputs and eliminating unintended state changes.</p>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSC203P",
   "LEVEL": 2,
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO1",
    "PLO2"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p>A financial tool requires deterministic calculations without side effects. What makes functional programming suitable here?</p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 107,
   "TYPE": "sq",
   "key": 9361
  },
  {
   "_id": 9362,
   "ANSWER": "<p>Functions such as <code data-end=\"3531\" data-start=\"3526\">map</code>, <code data-end=\"3541\" data-start=\"3533\">filter</code>, and <code data-end=\"3555\" data-start=\"3547\">reduce</code> abstract common data operations, enabling concise, readable, and reusable transformations</p>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSC203P",
   "LEVEL": 2,
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO1",
    "PLO2"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p>A dataset undergoes multiple filtering and transformation steps. How do higher-order functions contribute to this task?</p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 107,
   "TYPE": "sq",
   "key": 9362
  }
 ],
 "lq": [
  {
   "_id": 9380,
   "ANSWER": "<p data-end=\"3359\" data-start=\"3183\">List&lt;Double&gt; incomes = Arrays.asList(400000.0, 600000.0, 1000000.0);<br />\nList&lt;Double&gt; taxes = incomes.stream()<br />\n&nbsp; &nbsp; .map(income -&gt; income &gt; 500000 ? income * 0.2 : income * 0.1)<br />\n&nbsp; &nbsp; .collect(Collectors.toList());</p>\n\n<p data-end=\"3359\" data-start=\"3183\">public static double computeTotalTax(List&lt;Double&gt; taxes, int index) {<br />\n&nbsp; &nbsp; if (index &gt;= taxes.size()) return 0;<br />\n&nbsp; &nbsp; return taxes.get(index) + computeTotalTax(taxes, index + 1);<br />\n}<br />\nNo mutable state is introduced, ensuring a <strong data-end=\"4822\" data-start=\"4807\">predictable</strong> and <strong data-end=\"4842\" data-start=\"4827\">thread-safe</strong> computation.</p>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSC203P",
   "LEVEL": 3,
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO1",
    "PLO2"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p data-end=\"613\" data-start=\"371\">Design a tax computation module for a financial application using <strong data-end=\"4014\" data-start=\"3988\">functional programming</strong> principles. Ensure immutability by using <strong data-end=\"4069\" data-start=\"4056\">recursion</strong> and <strong data-end=\"4100\" data-start=\"4074\">higher-order functions</strong>.</p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 107,
   "TYPE": "lq"
  }
